ck men labored without compensation, were repeatedly bought and sold, and were forced through beatings and physical torture to do the bidding of white masters for decades after the official abolition of American slavery.The neoslavery system exploited legal loopholes and federal policies that discouraged prosecution of whites for continuing to hold black workers against their wills.","pageCount":466,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"African Americans -- Civil rights -- History -- 19th century","sourceId":"source-open-library-slavery-by-another-name-the-re-enslavement-of-black-americans-from-the-civil-war-to-world-war-ii"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"African Americans -- Civil rights -- History -- 20th century","sourceId":"source-open-library-slavery-by-another-name-the-re-enslavement-of-black-americans-from-the-civil-war-to-world-war-ii"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"African Americans -- Employment -- History","sourceId":"source-open-library-slavery-by-another-name-the-re-enslavement-of-black-americans-from-the-civil-war-to-world-war-ii"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"African Americans -- Crimes against -- History","sourceId":"source-open-library-slavery-by-another-name-the-re-enslavement-of-black-americans-from-the-civil-war-to-world-war-ii"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"African American prisoners -- Social conditions","sourceId":"source-open-library-slavery-by-another-name-the-re-enslavement-of-black-americans-from-the-civil-war-to-world-war-ii"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Forced labor -- United States -- History","sourceId":"source-open-library-slavery-by-another-name-the-re-enslavement-of-black-americans-from-the-civil-war-to-world-war-ii"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Convict labor -- Unit